# Build context hygiene. Without this, `docker build .` uploads ~450 MB of node_modules
# to the daemon on every build — twice per CI run — and busts the layer cache whenever
# any ignored file changes.
#
# Every pattern is `**/`-prefixed. Docker's ignore patterns are ROOT-ANCHORED: a bare
# `.env` excludes only `./.env` and happily copies `apps/api/.env` into the image. That is
# a secret-leak vector, not a tidiness issue — verified by building a probe image and
# finding a nested env file inside it.

# Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image from lockfiles)
**/node_modules/
**/.pnpm-store/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# Build output
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.turbo/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets — belt and braces with .gitignore; a build context is not a git checkout
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# VCS, CI, docs, and tooling: none of it is needed to build a runnable image
.git/
.github/
docs/
*.md
!apps/api/app/domains/README.md

# Test and cache artifacts
**/coverage/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Local/editor
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.log
**/.vercel
**/.railway
